	(text "NOTES  (this sheet is used twice: USB Port 1 = 4xx, USB Port 2 = 5xx)\n1. Address straps are on the root sheet: port 1 ADCIN1 = LDO_3V3, ADCIN2 = GND (0x20);\n   port 2 ADCIN1 = ADCIN2 = GND (0x21). R405-R408 are DNP divider footprints for other options.\n2. Unused TPS25751 GPIOs tied to GND per datasheet (KiCad ERC flags this; expected).\n3. D402/D403 (24 V rated ESD) and C401/C402 right at the connector pins, before anything else.\n4. Kelvin-route ACP/ACN from R424 and SRP/SRN from R427; filter parts at the IC.\n5. Two of each bulk bank plus C430/C438 at the FETs; the rest under the power stage.\n6. I2Cc pull-ups go to this TPS25751's own LDO_3V3 (TI guidance).\n7. R430 = 10 A copper link to PACK_P (net-tie footprint, not a part); widen with zones.\n8. VAC is taken before R424 per TI typical application; DRV_SUP fed from REGN via R420.\n9. PPHV bulk (BQ25756 input bank) exceeds the 100 uF USB PD cSnkBulkPd: the TPS25751D sink switch soft-start limits\n   inrush (C x SS: 220 uF x 0.47 V/ms max = 0.1 A at SS setting 0).\n   Set PPHV soft-start to setting 0 or 1 in the TPS25751 configuration."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 459.74 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ceb64665-2f2a-4393-93d0-477f223ba49f")
	)
